<p>Marbella and Granada are closer together than many visitors assume — about 165 kilometers apart — and a private chauffeur transfer typically makes the crossing in around 2 hours, heading inland from the Costa del Sol through the mountains toward Granada's high plain. The route generally follows the A-7 or AP-7 east toward Málaga before cutting north on the A-45 and A-92, or takes a more direct inland line depending on traffic and road conditions on the day, always avoiding the need to backtrack through central Málaga.</p>
